  message: "Closed done (PR b498838c12). BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE — end-to-end dogfood (hypergumbo survey, 2-file swift repo): doWork()'s untyped obj.create()/delete()/run() now emit unresolved external calls edges @0.40 (evidence_type=ast_call, meta.call_construct=method), 0 misbinds to the top-level create/delete/run (was @0.80 each); a param-typed receiver typed(c: Client) -> c.send() resolves to Client.send @0.85 (recall preserved via the new param-type threading). Unit tests: TestSwiftInvFahubReceiverGating (4: no-misbind / canonical-unresolved-shape / param-typed-resolves / typed-unresolvable-stamps-hint) + full 168-test swift suite (incl. the WI-huzuv dst_ref sweep) green; swift.py 100% coverage. FIX (leaf-only, INV-nilud-conform): same shape as the Scala facet — gate the bare-name binds behind receiver_hint is None; a method call with an unresolvable receiver emits py.py's unresolved shape (+ receiver_type_hint when the type is known). RECALL RECOVERY: threaded function/method PARAMETER types into var_types — Swift previously tracked ONLY property-declaration types (let x: T) and dropped ALL param types, so a func handle(client: Client) receiver was untracked and misbound; now param-typed receivers resolve. WI-huzuv PRESERVED: the gate carries the external dst_ref (module_path from receiver/import-alias/type) so a module-qualified call HelpersModule.doWork() keeps its structured reference — the Scala facet did not hit this because its WI-huzuv test uses a bare call, not a receiver call. No CORE/linker change. DEFERRED: the Swift left-to-right MRO walker (_walk_left_to_right, FUTURE) for Step-2 inherited-method recovery. INV-fahub stays violated (bakeoff-gated); D facet (WI-situj) remains."  # 9aed
